  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_773e4f48b79a48d3878ef579507de07f",
      "statement": "RootFollowStage lands the character on a target by rewriting bone 0's velocity channels rather than by moving the character's Transform, because the component derives the frame's own motion from those channels when it advances the character; a Transform written beside that integration would be a correction nothing downstream could blend, cap or disable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Stages/RootFollowStage.cs#L7-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fa44d9ccdf0f8ac810a03c064bf0f8a8b9009c253ea2742c3f369e08c5708e46:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Stages/RootFollowStage.cs#L94-L133",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d0c63a219e44ca6b1bf95fd4e6a559e22b96e27c622eb644b8591dc7491840f3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cfcc4af05629409583384473826ad34e",
      "statement": "The correction is the residual left after subtracting the motion the pose was already going to produce from the gap to the target, damped by a half-life and optionally capped; a zero half-life closes the whole gap in one tick and needs no special case, because the implicit damper's exponential is already indistinguishable from one there.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Stages/RootFollow.cs#L20-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:12d434d56bed06503d36b11425f314cb78f7f3e19b82499378fe81c86071d91e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Utils/Spring.cs#L27-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a58fa6c44b7e2cc92c1a04fe0db50017954ec33de27e875b20e284ddbf8f7513:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4b3dd450958447cab95429fdfff8a7a0",
      "statement": "Root following works in the ground plane only: the character frame is ground-projected by construction, so a correction routed through bone 0's velocity can never change the character's height, and a target above or below it is followed in x and z and ignored in y.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Stages/RootFollow.cs#L60-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a6051b960faf465093bcb30bb185d60f61f65ff1561fdd70312589f544eeebb3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/SimulationFrame.cs#L63-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4bc1ba11f67b87dc9ae356c8a4d65fac0d70cef51106837296086cd15038e4f0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5dfa00728959401fb22334717a30fa98",
      "statement": "RootFollowStage must run after Inertialization, because that blend smooths the pose stream and would otherwise smooth the correction away with it; it also goes inert, with a warning, when its target is null, is a child of the character, or when rootPositionsMask is off and the component therefore never integrates anything.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Stages/RootFollowStage.cs#L54-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:008cf2dce5fc3aabe46b97cdc592461d697effa9c386202e306bfe6288b26510:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Stages/RootFollowStage.cs#L14-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb80d10ed24472cd5fb83f656077a60b222b410baabc419fd688e4a901ff63f5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f1ba649a01614b7f8128160ad517bc74",
      "statement": "A target's Transform is not always where the target is — a spline follower's point travels along its path while its object stays put — so IFrameTarget lets a target answer for its own position and facing, and alignTargetOnInit is skipped for such a target since it decides where it is.",
      "evidence": [
